        <mxCell id="nota" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Domain rules and design decisions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Only a human User can create a Question. Only the author of the Question can accept answers.&lt;br&gt;• There can be several accepted answers. A Question has one Category and 0..* Tags.&lt;br&gt;• addAnswer() receives an AuthorFactory and gets the Author with createAuthor(): Question does not know whether the author is human or AI.&lt;br&gt;• Answer only knows the Author interface. The factories return an existing author (current user or registered agent).&lt;br&gt;• Vote is a separate class: a User casts only one Vote per Post. score is derived (sum of the Votes, +1 / -1).&lt;br&gt;• Automatic answer: if the Question has the trigger Tag (&quot;ia-help&quot;) or the time without answers has expired, the service gets the text with LLMStrategy.generate(prompt) and calls Question.addAnswer(text, aiAgentFactory).&lt;br&gt;• The strategy is interchangeable and stays decoupled from the domain." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="820" x="800" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
